virglrenderer: no swizzle on a sampler in the GLSL

What: a TGSI sampler source with a swizzle (TEX ..., SAMP[0].wwww) was written
into GLSL as "fssamp0.wwww". The swizzle is now left out, as gallium's own
translators (tgsi_to_nir) ignore it: a sampler is not a vector.
Why: Mesa's VA-API video compositor (vl_compositor_gfx.c,
create_frag_shader_yuv) reads the alpha that way. The Mac refused the shader
("Swizzle of non-vector primitive sampler2DArray"), so its draws were skipped
and every frame VA-API converted to RGB stayed black: Google Chrome's
hardware decoder converts each frame to ARGB (its "1-copy" path on GL), so
YouTube in hardware showed nothing.
Upstreamable; not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-core-glsl-shaders.c "swizzle on a sampler (Mesa's
video compositor)" (fails without: the GLSL has "fssamp0." and the Mac's
OpenGL refuses it).
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
@@ -5237,20 +5237,22 @@
          break;
       }
       case TGSI_FILE_SAMPLER: {
+         /* A sampler is not a vector: its swizzle (Mesa's video compositor writes
+          * SAMP[0].wwww) means nothing, as in gallium's own translators. In GLSL
+          * it is an error ("Swizzle of non-vector primitive"). */
          const char *cname = tgsi_proc_to_prefix(ctx->prog_type);
          if (ctx->info.indirect_files & (1 << TGSI_FILE_SAMPLER)) {
             int basearrayidx = lookup_sampler_array(ctx, src->Register.Index);
             if (src->Register.Indirect) {
                char index[64];
-               strbuf_fmt(src_buf, "%ssamp%d[%s]%s", cname, basearrayidx,
-                          clamped_index(index, src->Indirect.Index, src->Register.Index - basearrayidx,
-                                        sampler_array_size(ctx, basearrayidx)),
-                          swizzle);
+               strbuf_fmt(src_buf, "%ssamp%d[%s]", cname, basearrayidx,
+                          clamped_index(index, src->Indirect.Index, src->Register.Index - basearrayidx,
+                                        sampler_array_size(ctx, basearrayidx)));
             } else {
-               strbuf_fmt(src_buf, "%ssamp%d[%d]%s", cname, basearrayidx, src->Register.Index - basearrayidx, swizzle);
+               strbuf_fmt(src_buf, "%ssamp%d[%d]", cname, basearrayidx, src->Register.Index - basearrayidx);
             }
          } else {
-            strbuf_fmt(src_buf, "%ssamp%d%s", cname, src->Register.Index, swizzle);
+            strbuf_fmt(src_buf, "%ssamp%d", cname, src->Register.Index);
          }
          sinfo->sreg_index = src->Register.Index;
       } break;
